+### Import tickets: `POST /tickets/import`
+
+```json
+{ "tickets": [
+  { "title": "VPN drops every hour", "requester": "maria@example.com", "priority": "high" },
+  { "title": "Badge reader stuck", "requester": "li@example.com" }
+] }
+```
+
+Each item is what `POST /tickets` takes, at most 5000 of them. Answers 201 with the new ids in the given order:
+
+```json
+{ "created": 2, "ids": ["T-0001", "T-0002"] }
+```
+
+Each imported ticket is recorded and its requester is notified just as when one ticket is created. If any item is
+invalid, none are created: 400 `invalid`, and the message names the first invalid item by its index in the array
+(0 for the first).
